        "original_id": "7d923f45-c267-541b-a660-0838a8917f7d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bill Murray, Frances McDormand, Richard Jenkins, Zoe Kazan, Jane Anderson, Breckin Meyer, Jennifer Love Hewitt\n- Works: Olive Kitteridge, Saturday Night Live, Garfield: The Movie, Meatballs, Caddyshack, Stripes, Tootsie, Ghostbusters, Scrooged, Ghostbusters II, What About Bob?\n- Places: Maine\n- Awards: Emmy Award\n\nFacts:\n- Bill Murray first gained exposure on Saturday Night Live, and those performances earned him his first Emmy Award.\n- Bill Murray later starred in the comedy films Meatballs (1979), Caddyshack (1980), Stripes (1981), Tootsie (1982), Ghostbusters (1984), Scrooged (1988), Ghostbusters II (1989), and What About Bob?\n- Olive Kitteridge is an HBO miniseries set in Maine.\n- Frances McDormand played the title character in the HBO miniseries Olive Kitteridge.\n- Richard Jenkins played Olive Kitteridge's loving husband Henry Kitteridge in Olive Kitteridge.\n- Zoe Kazan played Denise Thibodeau in Olive Kitteridge.\n- Bill Murray played Jack Kennison in Olive Kitteridge.\n- Jane Anderson won an Emmy Award for writing the screenplay for the 2014 miniseries Olive Kitteridge.\n- Garfield: The Movie starred Breckin Meyer as Jon Arbuckle and Jennifer Love Hewitt as Dr. Liz Wilson.\n- Bill Murray voiced Garfield in Garfield: The Movie.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
